     1→# Bionic Skills: Performance vs Competence Tracking
     2→
     3→**Plan:** Phase 3 of Bionic Skills Research Grounding
     4→**Effort:** 8 hours over Weeks 5-6
     5→**Priority:** CRITICAL (Model treats performance as competence - misses skill erosion)
     6→**Research TRL:** 8 (Well-documented in educational research)
     7→**Master Plan:** `plans/bionic-skills-research-grounding.md` §Phase 3
     8→**Master Roadmap:** `plans/MASTER_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md` §AI-Assisted Skills Enhancement →Phase 3
     9→**Related Plans:**
    10→- Phase 2: `plans/bionic-skills-phase-transition.md` (low competence → displacement risk)
    11→- Phase 4: `plans/bionic-skills-economic-distribution.md` (competence gaps → wage bargaining)
    12→
    13→---
    14→
    15→## Problem Statement
    16→
    17→**Current Model Limitation:**
    18→The existing `bionicSkills.ts` treats AI-assisted **performance** as equivalent to true **competence**. A worker who produces code 55% faster with Copilot is assumed to have improved their coding skill by 55%. This contradicts extensive research showing:
    19→
    20→**Performance ≠ Competence**
    21→
    22→- AI assistance boosts immediate output (performance)
    23→- BUT: Long-term skill retention (competence) depends on how AI is used
    24→- Without human scaffolding (teaching, feedback), "illusion of understanding" emerges
    25→- Workers can lose underlying skills they're no longer practicing
    26→
    27→---
    28→
    29→## Research Foundation
    30→
    31→### Primary Research:
    32→
    33→**"Illusion of Understanding" (Cognitive Research, 2024)**
    34→- Students using AI tutors scored 48-127% higher on immediate tests
    35→- But: Scores "plummeted" on retention tests weeks later
    36→- Mechanism: AI provides answers without building mental models
    37→- Source: Cognitive Research: Principles and Implications journal
    38→
    39→**"AI Inhibits On-the-Job Learning" (MDPI, 2023)**
    40→- Workers using AI tools showed reduced skill development over time
    41→- "Automation complacency" - over-reliance on AI suggestions
    42→- Knowledge workers became less capable without AI assistance
    43→- Source: MDPI Behavioral Sciences journal
    44→
    45→**"Scaffolding Matters" (Frontiers in Psychology, 2024)**
    46→- AI + human teaching support > AI alone
    47→- Students with instructor guidance retained 80% of skills
    48→- Students with AI-only assistance retained 40% of skills
    49→- Mechanism: Human teaching creates conceptual understanding, AI alone creates pattern matching
    50→- Source: Frontiers in Psychology educational technology section
    51→
    52→### Additional Support:
    53→
    54→**Deskilling in Automation (Historical Pattern)**
    55→- Airline pilots: Autopilot → reduced manual flying skills → accident risk in emergencies
    56→- GPS navigation: Reduced spatial reasoning and wayfinding ability
    57→- Calculator use: Reduced mental math ability (documented since 1980s)
    58→- Source: Multiple studies, Journal of Applied Psychology, Transportation Research
    59→
    60→---
    61→
    62→## Implementation Design
    63→
    64→### 1. Add Competence Tracking (3 hours)
    65→
    66→**Extend Skills Interface:**
    67→```typescript
    68→interface BionicSkills {
    69→  // Existing (keep these)
    70→  communication: number;
    71→  analyticalThinking: number;
    72→  creativity: number;
    73→  programming: number;
    74→  technicalSkills: number;
    75→  overallEffectiveness: number;
    76→
    77→  // NEW: Competence tracking
    78→  competence: {
    79→    communication: number;         // True skill without AI
    80→    analyticalThinking: number;
    81→    creativity: number;
    82→    programming: number;
    83→    technicalSkills: number;
    84→    overall: number;
    85→  };
    86→
    87→  // NEW: Performance-competence gap
    88→  gaps: {
    89→    communication: number;         // performance - competence
    90→    analyticalThinking: number;
    91→    creativity: number;
    92→    programming: number;
    93→    technicalSkills: number;
    94→    overall: number;
    95→  };
    96→
    97→  // NEW: Retention factors
    98→  retention: {
    99→    scaffoldingQuality: number;    // 0-1, human teaching support
   100→    aiRelianceLevel: number;       // 0-1, how much work done by AI
   101→    monthsOfUse: number;           // Time using AI
   102→    retentionRate: number;         // How much learning sticks (0-1)
   103→  };
   104→}
   105→```
   106→
   107→**Initialize Competence:**
   108→```typescript
   109→function initializeCompetence(segment: SocietySegment): void {
   110→  if (!segment.skills) return;
   111→
   112→  // Initial competence = current performance (no gap yet)
   113→  segment.skills.competence = {
   114→    communication: segment.skills.communication,
   115→    analyticalThinking: segment.skills.analyticalThinking,
   116→    creativity: segment.skills.creativity,
   117→    programming: segment.skills.programming,
   118→    technicalSkills: segment.skills.technicalSkills,
   119→    overall: segment.skills.overallEffectiveness
   120→  };
   121→
   122→  // Initialize gaps (all zero initially)
   123→  segment.skills.gaps = {
   124→    communication: 0,
   125→    analyticalThinking: 0,
   126→    creativity: 0,
   127→    programming: 0,
   128→    technicalSkills: 0,
   129→    overall: 0
   130→  };
   131→
   132→  // Initialize retention factors
   133→  segment.skills.retention = {
   134→    scaffoldingQuality: getScaffoldingQuality(segment),
   135→    aiRelianceLevel: 0,  // Grows as AI capability increases
   136→    monthsOfUse: 0,
   137→    retentionRate: 0.7   // Base 70% retention
   138→  };
   139→}
   140→
   141→function getScaffoldingQuality(segment: SocietySegment): number {
   142→  // Quality of human teaching/mentorship available to this segment
   143→  // Based on education access, workplace training quality
   144→
   145→  const qualityByStatus: Record<string, number> = {
   146→    'elite': 0.85,         // High-quality education, mentorship
   147→    'professional': 0.70,  // Good workplace training
   148→    'middle': 0.55,        // Moderate training resources
   149→    'working': 0.35,       // Limited training, learning-by-doing
   150→    'precariat': 0.20      // Minimal support, self-taught
   151→  };
   152→
   153→  return qualityByStatus[segment.economicStatus] || 0.50;
   154→}
   155→```
   156→
   157→---
   158→
   159→### 2. Update Performance vs Competence (3 hours)
   160→
   161→**Monthly Update Logic:**
   162→```typescript
   163→function updateCompetenceTracking(state: GameState): void {
   164→  const avgAICapability = getAverageAICapability(state);
   165→
   166→  state.society.segments?.forEach(segment => {
   167→    if (!segment.skills) return;
   168→
   169→    const retention = segment.skills.retention;
   170→    retention.monthsOfUse++;
   171→
   172→    // Calculate AI reliance level
   173→    // Higher AI capability → more reliance (assuming access)
   174→    const aiAccess = segment.aiAccess || 0;
   175→    retention.aiRelianceLevel = aiAccess * Math.min(avgAICapability / 2.0, 1.0);
   176→    // Caps at 1.0 (full reliance) when AI reaches 2.0 capability
   177→
   178→    // Calculate retention rate based on scaffolding and reliance
   179→    // High scaffolding + moderate reliance → good retention
   180→    // Low scaffolding + high reliance → poor retention
   181→    retention.retentionRate = calculateRetentionRate(
   182→      retention.scaffoldingQuality,
   183→      retention.aiRelianceLevel
   184→    );
   185→
   186→    // Update competence for each skill
   187→    updateSkillCompetence(segment, avgAICapability);
   188→
   189→    // Calculate gaps
   190→    segment.skills.gaps = {
   191→      communication: segment.skills.communication - segment.skills.competence.communication,
   192→      analyticalThinking: segment.skills.analyticalThinking - segment.skills.competence.analyticalThinking,
   193→      creativity: segment.skills.creativity - segment.skills.competence.creativity,
   194→      programming: segment.skills.programming - segment.skills.competence.programming,
   195→      technicalSkills: segment.skills.technicalSkills - segment.skills.competence.technicalSkills,
   196→      overall: segment.skills.overallEffectiveness - segment.skills.competence.overall
   197→    };
   198→  });
   199→}
   200→
   201→function calculateRetentionRate(scaffolding: number, reliance: number): number {
   202→  // Research-backed formula from Frontiers Psychology (2024)
   203→  // High scaffolding + moderate reliance = optimal (80% retention)
   204→  // Low scaffolding + high reliance = poor (30-40% retention)
   205→
   206→  const baseRetention = 0.50;  // 50% baseline
   207→
   208→  // Scaffolding bonus (up to +35%)
   209→  const scaffoldingBonus = scaffolding * 0.35;
   210→
   211→  // Reliance penalty (quadratic - hurts more at high reliance)
   212→  const reliancePenalty = Math.pow(reliance, 2) * 0.30;
   213→
   214→  // Scaffolding can partially offset reliance penalty
   215→  const netPenalty = reliancePenalty * (1 - scaffolding * 0.5);
   216→
   217→  return Math.max(
   218→    0.20,  // Minimum 20% retention (something always sticks)
   219→    Math.min(
   220→      0.90,  // Maximum 90% retention (some loss inevitable)
   221→      baseRetention + scaffoldingBonus - netPenalty
   222→    )
   223→  );
   224→}
   225→```
   226→
   227→**Skill Competence Evolution:**
   228→```typescript
   229→function updateSkillCompetence(segment: SocietySegment, aiCapability: number): void {
   230→  const skills = segment.skills!;
   231→  const retention = skills.retention;
   232→
   233→  // For each skill domain
   234→  const skillDomains: Array<keyof BionicSkills> = [
   235→    'communication', 'analyticalThinking', 'creativity',
   236→    'programming', 'technicalSkills'
   237→  ];
   238→
   239→  skillDomains.forEach(domain => {
   240→    const currentPerformance = skills[domain] as number;
   241→    const currentCompetence = skills.competence[domain as keyof typeof skills.competence] as number;
   242→
   243→    // Performance improvement from AI (current system - keep this)
   244→    const performanceGain = calculatePerformanceGain(currentCompetence, aiCapability, segment.aiAccess || 0);
   245→    const newPerformance = currentCompetence + performanceGain;
   246→
   247→    // Competence improvement (learning that sticks)
   248→    const competenceGain = performanceGain * retention.retentionRate;
   249→    const newCompetence = currentCompetence + competenceGain * 0.01;
   250→    // 1% of monthly gain converts to long-term competence
   251→
   252→    // Competence decay from disuse (if high AI reliance)
   253→    const disuseFactor = retention.aiRelianceLevel * 0.005;  // 0.5% per month at full reliance
   254→    const competenceDecay = currentCompetence * disuseFactor;
   255→
   256→    // Update
   257→    skills[domain] = newPerformance;
   258→    (skills.competence[domain as keyof typeof skills.competence] as number) = Math.max(
   259→      0.1,  // Min competence
   260→      newCompetence - competenceDecay
   261→    );
   262→  });
   263→
   264→  // Update overall effectiveness
   265→  skills.overallEffectiveness = (
   266→    skills.communication * 0.2 +
   267→    skills.analyticalThinking * 0.2 +
   268→    skills.creativity * 0.2 +
   269→    skills.programming * 0.2 +
   270→    skills.technicalSkills * 0.2
   271→  );
   272→
   273→  skills.competence.overall = (
   274→    skills.competence.communication * 0.2 +
   275→    skills.competence.analyticalThinking * 0.2 +
   276→    skills.competence.creativity * 0.2 +
   277→    skills.competence.programming * 0.2 +
   278→    skills.competence.technicalSkills * 0.2
   279→  );
   280→}
   281→```
   282→
   283→---
   284→
   285→### 3. Crisis Effects (2 hours)
   286→
   287→**AI Disruption Events:**
   288→```typescript
   289→function checkForCompetenceCrisis(state: GameState): void {
   290→  // If large performance-competence gaps emerge, trigger events
   291→
   292→  state.society.segments?.forEach(segment => {
   293→    if (!segment.skills) return;
   294→
   295→    const overallGap = segment.skills.gaps.overall;
   296→
   297→    // Moderate gap (30%+)
   298→    if (overallGap > 0.30 && !segment.competenceCrisisWarning) {
   299→      segment.competenceCrisisWarning = true;
   300→
   301→      addEvent(state, {
   302→        type: 'social',
   303→        severity: 'medium',
   304→        title: `Skill Erosion: ${segment.name}`,
   305→        description: `${segment.name} showing signs of skill erosion. Performance boosted ${(overallGap * 100).toFixed(0)}% by AI, but true competence lagging. Workers increasingly dependent on AI assistance.`,
   306→        effects: {
   307→          competenceGap: overallGap
   308→        }
   309→      });
   310→    }
   311→
   312→    // Severe gap (50%+)
   313→    if (overallGap > 0.50 && !segment.competenceCrisisActive) {
   314→      segment.competenceCrisisActive = true;
   315→
   316→      addEvent(state, {
   317→        type: 'crisis',
   318→        severity: 'high',
   319→        title: `⚠️ COMPETENCE CRISIS: ${segment.name}`,
   320→        description: `${segment.name} experiencing severe skill erosion. True competence ${(segment.skills.competence.overall * 100).toFixed(0)}% while AI-assisted performance ${(segment.skills.overallEffectiveness * 100).toFixed(0)}%. Workers unable to function without AI. Emergency retraining needed.`,
   321→        effects: {
   322→          competenceGap: overallGap,
   323→          retrainingUrgency: 1.0
   324→        }
   325→      });
   326→
   327→      // Increase QoL decline from anxiety/insecurity
   328→      segment.segmentQoL = Math.max(0, segment.segmentQoL - 0.1);
   329→    }
   330→  });
   331→}
   332→```
   333→
   334→**AI Outage Scenario:**
   335→```typescript
   336→function simulateAIOutage(state: GameState, durationMonths: number): void {
   337→  // What happens if AI systems become unavailable?
   338→  // Workers must rely on true competence, not AI-boosted performance
   339→
   340→  addEvent(state, {
   341→    type: 'crisis',
   342→    severity: 'destructive',
   343→    title: '🚨 AI SYSTEM OUTAGE',
   344→    description: `Major AI infrastructure failure. Systems offline for ${durationMonths} months. Productivity drops to baseline competence levels. Workers scrambling to compensate.`,
   345→    effects: { aiOutage: durationMonths }
